| ✅ | Feature flags (e.g., enabling/disabling debug mode, rate‑limit thresholds) are configurable via env vars. |
| ✅ | Log messages that reference configuration values use the dynamic variables, not literals. |
| ✅ | A `.env.example` file is kept in the repo documenting required variables (without real secrets). |
| ✅ | CI/CD pipelines inject the necessary env vars for each environment, never rely on hard‑coded defaults. |

---

**Bottom line:**  
The only hard‑coded runtime value in the present repository is the listening port (`3000`). Moving that (and any future configuration data) to environment variables is a best practice that enhances portability, security, and operational flexibility. If you plan to expand this project—adding databases, third‑party services, or authentication—make sure their credentials and URLs are also sourced from `process.env` (or a dedicated secret store).  

